# 48. Observability Access Control

Access to observability information must follow authorization rules.

For example:

```text
Engineer
→ infrastructure health

Security administrator
→ security telemetry

Operations user
→ operational system health

Clinical / response user
→ relevant operational telemetry
```

Users should not automatically receive unrestricted observability access.

---

# 49. Privacy

Observability systems can accidentally become repositories of sensitive information.

Therefore:

```text
Do not log unnecessary personal data.
Do not log credentials.
Do not log authentication secrets.
Do not log sensitive payloads by default.
Do not duplicate sensitive operational data unnecessarily.
```

---

# 50. Redaction

Sensitive information should be redacted or excluded from logs and telemetry where appropriate.

Examples:

```text
credentials
tokens
session secrets
unnecessary identifiers
sensitive payload fields
```

---

# 51. Observability Retention

Retention should be policy-driven.

Different data types may require different retention periods:

```text
