---

# 94. Final Architecture Principle

AEGIS must never give the appearance of certainty simply because its dashboard is functioning.

A beautifully rendered interface showing stale, incomplete, or corrupted information is more dangerous than an obvious system failure.

Therefore:

> **AEGIS must make the health, freshness, provenance, quality, uncertainty, and limitations of its information visible to the people relying on it.**

The system should never merely say:

```text
DATA: 72
```

It should be capable of answering:

```text
What is 72?

Where did it come from?

When was it measured?

Is the source healthy?

Is the value current?

Has it been transformed?

Can we trust it?

What does it mean?

What does it NOT mean?
```

That is the standard required for a high-stakes bio-resilience system.
